# Isaac smoke PhysX monitoring and console log keys

## PhysX fail-closed (do not drop between revisions)

- Headless **and GUI** multi-target / Phase 7.5 playback smokes must subscribe
  to PhysX contact reports (`TipBodyContactMonitor` / equivalent) for the
  entire episode motion.
- **Prohibited body–target contact** fails the episode (`body_contact`) and
  must fail suite acceptance when `failed_episodes > max_failed_episodes`.
- Tip/body contact evidence must be printed on the **streamed smoke console
  (stdout)** with the normative tag `phase7_2_physx:` (not only Kit UI
  messages). Absence of these lines when contacts occur is a defect.
- Kit/PhysX engine overlap or collide errors (including spawn-time
  penetrating statics from stale prims) must fail the smoke when detected;
  do not treat them as ignorable Kit noise.
- Never weaken, skip, or comment out PhysX fail-closed checks to obtain a
  green GUI/headless run.

## Inter-episode target field clear

- Each episode’s incremental (or fixed) field is planned from a **clear
  field**. Before spawning an episode’s targets — and before each
  `--no-auto-exit` replay pass — remove **all** prims under
  `/World/Phase7_2/Targets`, not only the next episode’s target ids.
  Disjoint candidate ids across episodes make partial clears leave
  overlapping cubes and silent PhysX collisions.

## Console log glossary

- Canonical key meanings live in [`docs/console_log_keys.md`](../../docs/console_log_keys.md).
- **Whenever** console tags, `key=value` tokens, or report JSON fields are
  added, renamed, removed, or change meaning, update that glossary in the
  **same change set**, plus `CHANGES.md` and the applicable phase report /
  `spec.md` when the tag is normative.
- Prefer stable tag prefixes (`phase7_2_playback:`, `phase7_2_physx:`,
  `phase7_5_populate:`, …) over ad-hoc unmarked prints for smoke-critical
  evidence.
